# Line endings for anything that runs ON THE DEVICE.
#
# Android's /system/bin/sh rejects CRLF outright, and the failure does not look
# like a line-ending problem: a script with CRLF fails partway through with an
# error about a command name that has an invisible \r glued to it.
#
# The reflexive fix makes it worse. Toybox sed does not interpret \r, so the
# standard guard `sed -i 's/\r$//'` degrades to `s/r$//` and silently strips a
# trailing literal 'r' from every line of the file. That is how a build script's
# `/app/server` once became `/app/serve`, so the application never landed in the
# image while `docker commit` still reported success.
#
# Pinning eol=lf here means the bytes are correct before they ever leave git,
# whoever clones and whatever their core.autocrlf happens to be. Detection still
# belongs at the install step (deploy/install-device-scripts.sh aborts on a CR);
# this is the belt to that suspenders.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.rc        text eol=lf
*.hujson    text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf
